# Emulator-only configuration.
#
# Firebase reads `.env.local` only for the local emulator suite, never deploys
# it, and lets it take precedence over `.env`. **It overrides only the keys it
# defines** — anything omitted falls through to `functions/.env`, which is
# gitignored and holds the real credentials. That fall-through is what lets this
# file be committed: it never needs to contain a secret.
#
# `.gitignore` carries a deliberate exception for this path.

FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID=hl-genesis

# Emulator-only. A state sealed with the production key would be openable by the
# production callback, so this is deliberately not that key.
OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=emulator-only-state-secret-not-used-anywhere-real


# ============================================================================
# MODE B — the REAL HighLevel, reached through the ngrok tunnel   ← ACTIVE
# ============================================================================
# HL_CLIENT_ID, HL_CLIENT_SECRET and HL_VERSION_ID are deliberately NOT set
# here. They fall through to functions/.env, so the real credentials stay out
# of git. HL_AUTHORIZE_BASE and HL_API_BASE are also unset, so config.ts uses
# its defaults — the real marketplace and services hosts.
#
# The only things that must differ from a deployed run are the redirect and the
# allowed origin, because the browser is on the tunnel rather than on the
# deployed site.
#
# Requires, once, on the marketplace app under Advanced Settings -> Auth:
#     Redirect URL = https://docile-comment-charging.ngrok-free.dev/api/oauth/callback
# byte for byte. HighLevel matches it exactly.
#
# And open the app at the tunnel URL, not at localhost — the callback answers a
# *relative* redirect, so it resolves against whichever origin the browser is on.

HL_REDIRECT_URI=https://docile-comment-charging.ngrok-free.dev/api/oauth/callback
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://docile-comment-charging.ngrok-free.dev,http://localhost:5173


# ============================================================================
# MODE A — stubbed HighLevel   (swap back by uncommenting this block and
#                               commenting out MODE B above)
# ============================================================================
# The stand-in is served by the `api` function itself and mounted only under the
# emulator, so the loop runs offline: no network, no sandbox, no expiring codes.
#
# **Every automated test runs MODE A regardless of what is set here** — the test
# scripts point the bases at the fake themselves, because CLAUDE.md requires
# HighLevel stubbed in CI and the suite must not depend on a sandbox that
# expires in six months.
#
# HL_AUTHORIZE_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:5001/demo-genesis/asia-south1/api/__fake-hl
# HL_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:5001/demo-genesis/asia-south1/api/__fake-hl
# HL_CLIENT_ID=emulator-client-id
# HL_CLIENT_SECRET=emulator-client-secret
# HL_VERSION_ID=emulator-version-id
# HL_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/api/oauth/callback
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
